<title>RUSSIA: Russia to sell oil company stakes in 1997.</title>
<headline>Russia to sell oil company stakes in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia will sell 19.68 pct of oil holding company NGK Slavneft in an investment tender this year, the Federal Property Fund said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It also announced it would sell 22 percent of AO Yaroslavnefteprodukt, a Slavneft subsidiary, at a special auction.</p>
<p>The Fund released the following details of a number of oil and other companies planned for sale this year--  </p>
<p>	 PLANNED SALES BY RUSSIAN PROPERTY FUND IN 1997</p>
<p> Company			   Share packet	 Type of sale</p>
<p>				   as pct of capital</p>
<p> NGK Slavneft			19.68	   investment tender</p>
<p>(Megionneftegaz </p>
<p>is main production unit)</p>
<p> AO Yaroslavnefteprodukt	 22.00	   special auction</p>
<p>(Slavneft subsidiary)</p>
<p> NK Norsi-oil			40.00	   investment tender</p>
<p> AO Nizhegorodnefteorgsintez   15.00	   investment tender</p>
<p>(Norsi-oil subsidiary)</p>
<p> AO Nizhegorodnefteprodukt     18.30	   investment tender</p>
<p>  (Norsi-oil subsidiary)	 23.40	   special auction</p>
<p>NK SIBUR (Sibirsky Uralsky</p>
<p>  neftegaz)			  34.00	   investment tender</p>
<p> Rosgosstrakh (insurance)	50.00	   special auction</p>
<p> NK LUKoil  LKOH.RTS	    15.00	   investment tender</p>
<p> NK LUKoil  0#LKOH.RUO	   4.97	   options</p>
<p> Arkhangelsky TsBK (paper/     20.00	   special auction</p>
<p>cellulose)</p>
<p> AO Svyazinvest (telecom	 49.00	   commercial tender</p>
<p>  holding company)				   (two packets)</p>
<p> Novorossiskoe Morskoe	    5.34	   special auction</p>
<p>Parokhodstvo (Novoship</p>
<p>shipping company)</p>
<p> Novomoskovskbytkhim	     20.00	   special auction</p>
<p>  (detergents)					 (bids accepted</p>
<p>							   until Feb 28, 1997)</p>
<p>Notes -</p>
<p>The Fund did not give any dates for the sales in a press release except as mentioned above.</p>
<p>Fund Deputy Chairman Vladimir Malinan said earlier on Thursday that Russia also intended to sell 1.5 to 2.0 percent of Unified Energy System (UES)  after about six months.</p>
<p>A special auction for two percent of Slavneft, jointly held by Russia and Belarus, will also be held in both Russia and Belarus, he said.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
